{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Repair bin/publish so publication atomically switches current while concurrent readers see only a complete previous or new release, with current remaining present and complete.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The repaired publisher creates a same-directory temporary symlink and atomically replaces current. Bounded concurrent tests performed 100 pre-restart and 40 post-restart switches, observing both releases across 1,556 reads with zero missing, incomplete, or invalid states. The final current target was complete release two.","evidence_ids":["cmd-471f2c9c64e84ccb","cmd-0923af395ef1404e","cmd-842cffdd7abe478b","cmd-e5e5033eedda496f"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Refuse any release missing MANIFEST and retain the prior current target when rejected.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Publishing releases/incomplete returned exit 65. Before and after rejection, the current target, symlink identity, and exposed content remained unchanged; this was confirmed both before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-198d0342ba70443c","cmd-842cffdd7abe478b"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Preserve both staged releases and keep rollback/publication to either complete release possible.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Release one and release two were each successfully activated, and all staged release checksums continued to match the preparation baseline through the final observation and restart.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-0923af395ef1404e","cmd-e3272ce5fa6c495e","cmd-35ea3bb727c34f5b","cmd-e5e5033eedda496f"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the existing platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The node remained on RHEL 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64 before and after the work and restart. The solution uses the installed POSIX shell and existing coreutils; the timeline contains no package installation or upgrade.","evidence_ids":["cmd-855621d381914d67","cmd-02ee9f08182045f0","cmd-35ea3bb727c34f5b","cmd-e5e5033eedda496f","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. The temporary defect reproduction was bounded to /tmp and removed (cmd-d3034c78011241c1); publisher replacement directly implemented the repair and included rollback cleanup (cmd-471f2c9c64e84ccb); live target switches directly tested atomicity and rollback and left release two current (cmd-0923af395ef1404e, cmd-e3272ce5fa6c495e, cmd-842cffdd7abe478b); and the reboot was required by the provider-wide protocol (cmd-f0dcb0d065fd4d56). Final checks found no repair artifacts or failed units, normal listeners, enforcing SELinux, and healthy package state. The restart protocol was complete: healthy pre-restart state and boot ID, acknowledged restart, a different post-restart boot ID independently corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered services, publisher, current release, and staged data.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d3034c78011241c1","cmd-471f2c9c64e84ccb","cmd-0923af395ef1404e","cmd-e3272ce5fa6c495e","cmd-3573bec6b49a43f8","cmd-f0dcb0d065fd4d56","cmd-7249a21874684d90","cmd-35ea3bb727c34f5b","cmd-842cffdd7abe478b","cmd-e5e5033eedda496f","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The release publisher now validates MANIFEST and atomically replaces current, both complete releases remain unchanged and selectable, rejection preserves the existing target, and the operating system and kernel were retained. The mandatory node-restart evidence is complete and coherent with the independent lifecycle observations.","limitations":["Continuous-reader behavior was assessed through bounded stress tests rather than an exhaustive observation of every instant; however, zero invalid observations across 1,556 reads and the directly captured same-filesystem atomic-replacement implementation provide strong corroboration."]}
